      {
        "id": 19885,
        "name": "usgrandprix",
        "username": "usgrandprix",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/u/85f322/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-04-25T15:47:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If the scene tracker iterates every time the environment takes a turn that favors larger groups. How do you guys compensate for that say in a 2 hero game?</p>\n<p>I know some things scale like x minions per hero&nbsp;but there are a lot of scenes where there are elements that don't scale &nbsp;and those elements usual are essential to succeeding.</p>\n<p>Say a scene essentially requires 10 overcome attempts to succeed. If the heroes concentrate on the overcomes this will take 2 heroes 5 rounds but it will take 5 heroes 2 rounds. 5 rounds&nbsp;of taking attacks without defense or fighting back is brutal compared to just 2.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:53:45.053Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 4,
        "readers_count": 3,
        "score": 0.8,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 19883,
        "topic_slug": "scaling",
        "display_username": "usgrandprix",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
